    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1305">

                <pb facs="0542" n="2244" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v09p2/pg2244"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">774.00/3–2554: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 1305<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Egypt (Caffery) to the
                        Department of State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d1305-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-03-25">March 25, 1954</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>1167. Following lengthy meeting with Naguib presiding, RCC announced today
                    following decisions:</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Political parties will be permitted organize immediately.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>RCC will not form political party.</item>
                    <pb facs="0543" n="2245" xml:id="pg2245"/>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>No one will be deprived of political rights.</item>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>Constituent Assembly will be freely elected (no appointees).</item>
                    <label>5.</label>
                    <item>RCC will turn over all powers to Constituent Assembly on July 24 and
                        consider revolution ended. President of Republic will be elected by Assembly
                        when it meets.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Caffery</hi></hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1305-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1305-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to London as telegram 386 and unnumbered to the Arab capitals, Tel Aviv,
                    Tripoli, and Khartoum.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
